+## Run And Results
 
-## Temporary External Watchdog Feeding
+The X6 fixture was verified on this P5 with the existing 2022 checkupdate:
+one --unpack completed and all five payload MD5 checks passed. This is fixture
+compatibility evidence, not a full DDR test. Recheck on boards with other tools.
+Never use --update or invoke checkupdate without arguments for these tests.
 
-The P5 TPL5010 external watchdog uses GPIO4_IO21 through the existing
-LED_Wtd_Done sysfs interface. wtd_feed.sh sends a 50 ms high pulse roughly
-every 10 seconds. This is a watchdog feeder, not a system wake-up script.
-It does not change boot configuration, kernel policies or firmware, and
-it does not run /bin/dog or modify its OOM/panic policies.
-
-If the earlier manual feeder (previously PID 196) still exists, verify its
-current PID using the command below and stop that PID with kill -TERM first.
-Do not blindly reuse an old PID. The helper refuses a detected manual feeder.
+Start temporary external watchdog feeding separately:
 
 ```sh
-ps | grep '[L]ED_Wtd_Done'
-# Only after confirming the PID belongs to the old manual feeder:
-# kill -TERM <confirmed-PID>
 sh wtd_feed.sh start
 sh wtd_feed.sh status
-sh ddr_test.sh --check --no-unpack
-sh ddr_test.sh -c 1 --memory 16 --seconds 60 --no-unpack
-```
-
-The helper uses setsid and nohup with detached stdin/stdout/stderr. Closing and reopening
-the serial terminal does not stop it. Keep the terminal open during DDR tests
-to capture unexpected resets. Runtime state and errors are in
-/mem/ddr-wtd-feed/ (RAM); they disappear after reboot. No PID is hardcoded.
-Start is idempotent; it does not launch another managed worker when one exists.
-Start/stop/status must use the same copy/path of the helper while it is running.
-
-```sh
-cat /mem/ddr-wtd-feed/feed.log
-sh wtd_feed.sh stop
-```
-
-WARNING: stopping feeding does NOT disable the external watchdog. The board
-may reset after its timeout. Restart promptly if continued operation is needed.
-The DDR suite does not automatically stop this feeder on completion/failure;
-feeding can mask a hung application, so this helper is only for controlled tests.
