-matching the original storage type rather than the previous eMMC extraction.
-The copied BIN/TAR inputs remain in RAM across rounds as in the original;
-they are removed at normal exit/interruption, not left in shared /tmp paths.
-Preflight requires a tmpfs/ramfs /tmp with at least 96 MiB available for the
-supplied fixtures. Each iteration runs extract, sync, MD5, delete, sync and
-usleep 100000. All requested iterations run even after a failed comparison;
-any extraction or MD5 failure makes the phase and final suite fail. Logs and
-one failed extraction sample per phase/round are kept on eMMC; unlike the
-original, unlimited failure backups are not accumulated in RAM.
-No install.sh, --update, recovery or flashing commands are invoked.
