-## Compatibility Boundaries
+-c 12 runs twelve COMPLETE rounds. Stressapptest alone totals 12 hours;
+memtester, unpack tests and delays make total duration longer than 12 hours.
+Keep the serial terminal connected. The test itself does not manage feeding.
+The feeder survives terminal disconnection but disappears after reboot.
+Stopping feeding does not disable the external watchdog and can cause a reset.
 
-Default test order, memory calculation, thread count, durations, unpack loop
-counts, per-iteration pauses, round numbering and numbered result format
-follow ../ddr_test.sh. P5-specific mount checks, thermal type selection,
-unique run directories, process cleanup and watchdog helper are retained.
-Failures are checked more strictly than the original's PASS grep / clipped
-memtester output: failure detection bugs are not compatibility requirements.
-No clean command deletes prior results, and no report-parser compatibility
-is claimed for the encrypted analysis tool. Tool versions and P5 hardware
-also differ; matching script parameters is not proof of identical load or
-DDR qualification. Host tests do not establish BIN/tool compatibility on P5.
